From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:46:11 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 142/202] Meridian: Arc's own shortcuts work in pages that take
 every key
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Editors and whiteboards (Google Docs, a canvas) preventDefault every
keydown, so ⇧⌘C, ⌘S, ⌘L and the rest never reached the browser. They are
reserved now, like the tab and space keys; editing keys, ⌘F, ⌘P, zoom
and ⌘[/] stay the page's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
---
 chrome/browser/ui/accelerator_table.cc | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/accelerator_table.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/accelerator_table.cc
index 219a29c2ee..d86bde5827 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/accelerator_table.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/accelerator_table.cc
@@ -436,6 +436,25 @@ constexpr int kReservedCommandIds[] = {
     IDC_MERIDIAN_SPACE_1 + 6,
     IDC_MERIDIAN_SPACE_1 + 7,
     IDC_MERIDIAN_SPACE_9,
+    // Meridian: so are the rest of Arc's own shortcuts. Editors and whiteboards
+    // (Google Docs, a canvas) take every ⌘ key they see; Arc's ⇧⌘C copies the
+    // link there all the same. Editing keys (⌘C/V/X/Z/A), ⌘F, ⌘P, zoom and
+    // ⌘[/] stay the page's, as in Chrome.
+    IDC_COPY_URL,
+    IDC_FOCUS_LOCATION,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_TOGGLE_SIDEBAR,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_TOGGLE_PIN,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_NEW_FOLDER,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_SPLIT,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_UNSPLIT,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_ARCHIVE,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_CLEAR_TODAY,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_ASK,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_CHAT,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_WORKBENCH,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_MISSION,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_COPY_MARKDOWN,
+    IDC_MERIDIAN_LITTLE_WINDOW,
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
     // On Android, pane navigation (F6 / Shift+F6) is also reserved so web
     // pages cannot trap keyboard focus.
